<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hanzhong</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hanzhong is a city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, in the basin of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-river">Han River</a> between the Qinling and Daba mountains. In 206 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> King of Han there, and from it Liu Bang broke out to found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, which took its name from the region. Its strategic passes were later contested between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bei">Liu Bei</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a>, who lost it to Liu Bei in 219.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hanzhong.jpg" alt="Hanzhong" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charlie fong · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Skyline_of_West_Hanzhong.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
